DECISION_NOTES = {
"property-management-virtual-assistant-tenant-communications":"Choose the provider only if routine messages become complete records and high-risk resident reports reach an accountable manager without administrative interpretation. The decisive evidence is a reproducible emergency handoff, controlled scripts, minimum vendor disclosure, and a manager-owned route for housing decisions.",
"construction-virtual-assistant-bid-coordination":"A credible bid coordinator leaves the estimator with a current package, visible addenda, an exception-focused brief, and proof of authorized submission. Decline a service that hides obsolete files, treats outreach as technical authority, or measures success without reconstructing the final portal check.",
"architecture-firm-virtual-assistant-submittal-tracking":"Approve the service when another project member can follow every submittal from receipt through linked revisions, professional review, authorized disposition, and return. Administrative neatness is secondary to preserved history, unambiguous ownership, and controls that prevent draft or conflicting technical comments from being issued.",
"saas-virtual-assistant-customer-onboarding-scope":"The onboarding role is ready when purchased outcomes, permissions, configurations, customer decisions, and unresolved risks survive a handoff into support. Meeting counts and login activity are supporting signals; they cannot replace evidence that the customer accepted the defined result and that custom requests reached their proper owners.",
"online-course-virtual-assistant-student-operations":"Select a provider that can reconcile enrollment and completion while protecting learner information and stopping at academic, payment, conduct, and accessibility decisions. The strongest pilot shows how a failed access event and a disputed completion record are corrected without exposing restricted data or inventing course policy.",
"membership-association-virtual-assistant-renewal-operations":"Renewal support earns expansion when term, amount, benefit access, consent, and payment can be traced for each member. The association should reject a workflow that improves campaign totals by extending unapproved benefits, overlooking payment differences, or merging records without reliable identity evidence.",
"nonprofit-virtual-assistant-donor-records-workflow":"The donor workflow should preserve intent from source evidence through reconciliation, acknowledgement, reporting, and recognition preferences. Expansion is appropriate only when restriction conflicts, identity uncertainty, noncash questions, and anonymity survive as owned exceptions instead of being cleaned away to speed receipt processing.",
"marketplace-seller-virtual-assistant-catalog-operations":"Catalog support is dependable when an approved attribute can be traced to every affected offer and the customer view matches the staged change. A provider should not pass if it treats accepted uploads as completion, repairs suppressions by evasion, or lets parent-level edits create unsupported claims across variations.",
"healthcare-virtual-assistant-referral-coordination":"A referral process is acceptable when the intended recipient receives the minimum authorized packet, patient choice is preserved, and completion returns to the practice as reconciled evidence. Clinical questions, new symptoms, and payer meaning must visibly leave the administrative lane without leaking health detail into general work systems.",
"accounting-firm-virtual-assistant-client-document-intake":"The professional handoff should expose what arrived, where it came from, what remains missing, and which conflicts require accounting judgment. A tidy folder is not success if duplicate reports, wrong-client material, unreadable files, or sufficiency decisions disappear from the engagement owner's view.",
"insurance-agency-virtual-assistant-policy-service-intake":"Policy-service intake is ready only when identity, authority, the client's exact request, licensed ownership, and the communication result can be reconstructed. Response speed never compensates for an unlicensed coverage statement, unsupported certificate wording, or a claims report routed without its original facts.",
"home-services-virtual-assistant-dispatch-intake":"Adopt the dispatch service when ordinary appointments reflect real capacity and observable safety reports reliably reach a trained owner through acknowledged escalation. The assistant's contribution is faithful intake and controlled scheduling, not remote diagnosis, priority changes, entry disclosure, or unapproved price promises.",
}

MORE_OPERATIONAL_REVIEWS = {
"nonprofit-virtual-assistant-donor-records-workflow":"Follow three gifts with different failure risks. For an online gift, compare the processor event, settlement, fee, CRM entry, acknowledgement, and campaign report; a timing difference remains an explained reconciling item until the deposit arrives. For a mailed check, retain its intake context, memo, deposit reference, and any campaign form expressing a different purpose. Fundraising and finance decide what the discrepancy means before acknowledgement wording is released. For a noncash item, record description and receipt while authorized owners retain acceptance and valuation statements. Then test identity and preference controls. Similar names, a household address, or a shared employer do not justify a merge. The reviewer should see the evidence used, retained source fields, correction history, and opt-out treatment. Generate both an internal reconciliation report and a public recognition list for an anonymous donor. Necessary internal detail stays under restricted access while the public export suppresses the name. Finally, correct one amount or designation and trace the correction through every downstream artifact. If the provider fixes only the CRM screen while an acknowledgement, campaign total, or event list stays wrong, the workflow has not closed the error. This review tests money, intent, identity, communication, and disclosure as connected obligations rather than isolated data-entry steps. It also gives managers a concrete basis for deciding which exceptions require immediate review, which can wait for routine reconciliation, and what evidence an assistant must retain before work is considered complete.",
"marketplace-seller-virtual-assistant-catalog-operations":"Run the pilot on a family with two colors, two sizes, a regional offer, and one bundle. Name the source for identifiers, dimensions, material, compatibility, imagery, price, stock, fulfillment, warranty, and safety information. When sources disagree, the assistant creates an exception naming both sources and the product owner instead of choosing the easiest value to upload. Change one parent-level attribute and preview every affected child. Inspect customer titles, bullets, selected images, purchasable combinations, price, and delivery language rather than trusting a clean spreadsheet. Next, introduce an unsupported certification or compatibility phrase. Publication must pause until the responsible owner supplies evidence and approves the exact claim; softening unsupported wording does not create a source. Preserve any platform suppression notice, listing state, attempted correction, approval, and result. Opening a duplicate listing to escape the notice should fail the exercise. Execute one authorized correction and compare the actual marketplace page across customer views. Confirm the selected variant shows approved facts and imagery, and retain a timestamped result tied to the change. An accepted feed can still yield a wrong live page because inheritance, caching, regional rules, or platform transformations intervene. The operating standard therefore closes on customer experience and keeps a rollback artifact for high-impact mistakes. The reviewer should also verify that unaffected variants remained stable, stock was not stranded under a detached child, and the audit record explains why the owner chose correction, retirement, or a new product identity.",
"healthcare-virtual-assistant-referral-coordination":"Test separate administrative and clinical complications. One case has a valid order but a missing destination requirement. The assistant identifies the missing item from an approved checklist without rewriting clinical intent or selecting extra chart material. A second case begins as an ordinary status call and then includes a new symptom. The assistant stops scheduling, preserves the patient's exact words, and uses the clinical escalation path without assigning urgency or giving advice. A third case receives a payer request whose consequences are unclear. The record can show authorization status and requested documentation, but trained staff interpret benefits, denial meaning, and response strategy. Across all cases, examine identity checks, patient choice, approved transfer channels, and minimum-necessary disclosure. A recipient asking for more information does not automatically gain the entire chart. A patient asking which specialist is best receives only options permitted by policy, with recommendations routed appropriately. Closure needs its own test: a fax confirmation or portal receipt proves transmission, not referral completion. Define whether the result is appointment acceptance, consultation documentation, returned findings, or another practice-owned event, and reconcile that result to the order. Inspect the general task board to ensure it contains operational status rather than copied clinical narrative. Access logs should show who opened the packet, corrections should retain their source, and unresolved clinical or payer questions should have named owners. This design lets administrative staff pursue missing paperwork and status efficiently while making every privacy, clinical, and coverage boundary visible.",
"accounting-firm-virtual-assistant-client-document-intake":"Use an engagement sample containing current records, an obsolete request, duplicate filenames, an unreadable scan, and another client's document. The request list identifies engagement, period, item, context, and responsible professional so an assistant does not imply that a copied prior-year list remains correct. Preserve original bytes, names, submitter context, receipt times, and secure channel. Working names may improve organization, but the index must lead back to provenance. Two payroll reports with different totals cannot be resolved by calling the later upload final. Both remain linked to an exception until the engagement owner identifies controlling evidence and records why. A file that opens and resembles a requested category is present, not professionally sufficient. Wrong-client information follows a security route: restrict access, preserve the event, notify the owner, and avoid multiplying exposure through email or chat. Test reminders too. They cite the unresolved item without sensitive attachments or requests for passwords. At handoff, another team member should open direct links for present items and separately see missing, superseded, unreadable, conflicting, and awaiting-review states. Corrections retain prior values and owners. The professional should be able to distinguish a client omission from an internal classification question and see which request was satisfied by which artifact. Sampling the index against storage also catches orphan files and rows pointing to replaced documents. This evidence trail lets accountants focus on interpretation while proving administrative organization did not erase chain of custody or turn intake status into an accounting conclusion.",
"insurance-agency-virtual-assistant-policy-service-intake":"Exercise five requests because a generic queue hides authority changes. Begin with a billing-status question permitted by approved guidance, then compare a request to add coverage. The latter reaches licensed staff with the client's words, policy reference, deadline, and verified identity intact. Have a representative call without clear authority; disclosure stops until the agency's verification path resolves the relationship. For a certificate request, insert wording that implies an unsupported interest or promise. Preparation may continue on objective fields, but disputed wording and issuance remain with the authorized reviewer. A new loss report tests another boundary: capture facts as stated, provide only approved immediate instructions, and route through the claims path without predicting coverage, fault, or settlement. Finally, ask whether a rented vehicle will be covered before pickup. The assistant must not search a fragment and announce an answer; preserve the licensed decision and communication result. Review response time alongside disclosure accuracy, routing, record completeness, corrections, and access removal. One quick material misstatement outweighs many routine messages handled within target. A second reviewer should reopen each item and identify the request, verification evidence, controlling source, administrative actions, licensed owner, outgoing communication, and unresolved next step. Sample attachments and recipient fields as well as notes, because an accurate summary can still accompany a disclosure error. If reconstruction depends on the assistant's memory, the agency has not built a safe policy-service record.",
"home-services-virtual-assistant-dispatch-intake":"Build the trial around capacity, safety, access, and commercial boundaries. An ordinary request maps to a service type, geography, duration assumption, skill requirement, and real dispatch opening. Remove a technician and see whether the assistant offers only authorized windows instead of displacing another job or promising an unconfirmed technician. A separate caller reports water near an electrical panel. The assistant applies the company's observable trigger, supplies only the approved emergency instruction, and alerts the on-call dispatcher; it does not diagnose the source, declare conditions safe, or bury the event in the next plumbing slot. Let the primary contact miss the alert so fallback and acknowledgement evidence are tested. Collect occupancy, pets, gates, parking, and permission according to policy, while keeping entry codes out of broadly visible calendars or chat. Ask for a firm repair price and warranty exception. Approved diagnostic fees and standard policies may be stated, but final scope, technical conclusions, discounts, warranties, and priority changes remain with authorized staff. End at a shift boundary with a late technician, parts dependency, customer callback, and open safety flag. The receiving dispatcher acknowledges each exception. Compare original customer wording, booking record, capacity source, alert attempts, access disclosure, pricing language, and handoff result. Also check whether the customer received an accurate window update after capacity changed and whether failed contact attempts remained visible to the next shift. That evidence shows whether the provider moves operations forward without converting a scheduling role into technical or commercial authority.",
}

MORE_ADDENDA = {
"nonprofit-virtual-assistant-donor-records-workflow":"Before approval, compare the batch total with bank evidence and inspect one acknowledgement chosen from each intake channel. Confirm that tax or recognition language came from an approved template, the donor's communication preference was applied at send time, and a held gift could not slip into an automated mailing while its restriction remained unresolved.",
"marketplace-seller-virtual-assistant-catalog-operations":"Include a rollback rehearsal for a published attribute error. Record which offers are paused, which source restores the former value, who approves the correction, and how customer-visible recovery is confirmed. The provider should distinguish correcting catalog truth from suppressing evidence of the original mistake, since the latter makes recurrence harder to diagnose. Reconcile one order placed during the error window so customer support knows which buyer saw which representation and which owner decides any remedy.",
"healthcare-virtual-assistant-referral-coordination":"Ask the receiving office to reject one incomplete packet and return a specific reason. The assistant should connect that response to the original referral, obtain the missing approved item, retransmit through the controlled channel, and keep both attempts visible. Clinical staff decide whether the delay or new information changes care instructions. Confirm that the patient receives only the status language approved for that stage and knows which clinical contact handles care questions.",
"accounting-firm-virtual-assistant-client-document-intake":"Finally, revoke a temporary intake account and test retrieval by the permanent engagement team. The files, exception states, correspondence history, and professional decisions must remain available under firm ownership, while the former assistant can no longer open client material. This proves that continuity and least access survive staffing changes. Compare the final index with the engagement request list and have the professional sign off on remaining gaps rather than allowing an administrative closed status to imply readiness for accounting work.",
"insurance-agency-virtual-assistant-policy-service-intake":"Add a correction exercise in which an earlier administrative message used the wrong billing date. The assistant should notify the designated reviewer, preserve the original communication, issue only the approved correction to the verified recipient, and update related tasks. The record must not suggest that correcting an administrative fact grants authority to reinterpret coverage. Review any automation that copied the wrong date into reminders or service tickets, stop further sends, and document which recipients require correction. The licensed owner should separately decide whether the error affected a coverage-related communication or customer decision. Inspect the service register afterward for duplicate open items, because a correction sent through a second ticket can separate the licensed response from the original request and leave later reviewers with an incomplete history.",
"home-services-virtual-assistant-dispatch-intake":"Reopen a completed booking after the customer changes access instructions and reports a new hazard. The workflow should protect the new entry detail, reactivate the safety route, notify the assigned operational owner, and prevent the old completion state from hiding the change. Dispatch history should show what changed, when, and who accepted responsibility.",
}

